ts": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn9le15ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le15ob11re2img02.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn9le15ob11re2img02.jpg", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "engenn9le15ob11re2img02.jpg", "text": "<p>It has been said that \u201cmoney doesn't buy happiness.\u201d A good number of celebrated artists and thinkers might suggest that fame doesn't buy happiness either, and that had they known the costs of their stardom, they might have chosen a different career path altogether.</p>\nSome, like Luciano Pavarotti, have succeeded in putting their celebrity to good use. Pavarotti was lauded by the press for performing humanitarian concerts aimed at raising money for people in areas of conflict. For others, however, fame was more of a curse than a blessing.", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn9le15ob11re2img02.jpg", "text": "Pioneers such as surrealist painter Salvador Dali were labeled eccentrics and received more than their share of bad press. Trailblazing mathematician Ada Lovelace was hounded by rumor and scandal throughout her entire career as a female in a male-dominated profession. Even venerated celebrities are not immune. In fact, the bigger the star, the more sensationalized the rumors seem to be. To this day, an urban legend is being circulated about the burial of Walt Disney, who many people believe lies frozen under a ride at Disneyland. These libelous attacks must have been a constant source of worry for the celebrities and their families.", "time": "32000", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn9le15ob11re2img03.jpg", "text": "And these examples don't even represent the worst case scenario. In some cases, fame may have directly led to an untimely death. It has been speculated that Wolfgang Mozart could have been murdered by a jealous counterpart, and Harry Houdini is said to have been killed by an overzealous fan, who gave him a punch to the stomach.", "time": "72500", "id": 3}]}}], "id": 1}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "type": "sena"}